  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC): Corruption Landscape Evaluation and Assessment of Risks: Unveiling Vulnerabilities in Regulatory Framework and Practices that Enable Corruption and Undermine Business Climate (CLEAR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To support tax authorities and stakeholders in developing a shared understanding of corruptionrisks in tax reassessments. 2) To ensure that tax authorities and stakeholders are committed to integrating assessment results into reform and decision-making processes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: The Ministry of Justice, the Ministry of Planning, and the Federation of Congolese Enterprises (F&#xe9;d&#xe9;ration des entreprises du Congo &#x2013; FEC)  Indirect beneficiaries: Investors, citizens and civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to foster a stable and enabling environment for private sector development, trade, and investment in the DRC by reducing corruption risks of tax reassessment practices.</narrative>
  </description>
